Z||000000||Black88GT||08-04-2000||10:53 AM||||My goal is to make this Fiero as reliable as I can for the longest time possible.  So far, here is what I have (soon to be installed)....<P>3.4 from '95 Firebird - 7k miles, brand new Fel Pro gasket conv. set<BR>AC Delco Battery Cables<BR>AC Delco Rapidfire spark plugs<BR>AC Delco Starter<BR>New Oil Pump (carparts.com)<BR>Fram Oil filter<BR>New Heater Core (carparts.com)<BR>Distributor Cap from AutoZone.<BR>Fairly new battery (3k miles)<BR>Fairly new clutch (4k miles)<BR>Radiator<P><BR>I was thinking Ignition stuff but I am saving up for the Jacobs setup.  Fuel Pumps are too expensive to just replace for the hell of it, I will wait on that one.  Especially with all the talk about them on the forum, I want to find the best one.<P>So, what does everyone think? Anything else? I might go and get a distributor rotor too, depending on price.<P>thanks,<BR>jeff<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mshill||08-04-2000||10:58 AM||||Replace all of the coolant hoses (two in front, two or three on back) as these will now feel the pressure since you have a new radiator and heater core without holes.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||08-04-2000||06:02 PM||||The Jacobs ignition system is over $300, the MSD 6AL is about $180. The difference you will get between the MSD and the Jacobs ignition systems is nothing. The MSD is a very reliable and proven ignition system and in my opinion is a better deal than the Jocobs ignition system. The fieros ignition system is really a very good system except for the coil so if you just upgrade your stock coil to an MSD or Accel coil your car would pull strong up to the redline.<P>I know that the Jocobs company makes there system look really good on paper but I have researched ignition systems and read about dynos done with them and I think that the Jocobs is way overpriced for what you get from it. You would get the same benefit form the MSD 6AL for less. Its about a 5 hp gain only at the upper RPM levels and about 4 ft lb.’s of torque.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 08-04-2000).]||||reg||1
